f="#how-do-you-decorate-a-bookshelf-without-it-looking-cluttered">How do you decorate a bookshelf without it looking cluttered?</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#how-many-books-should-go-on-each-shelf">How many books should go on each shelf?</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#what-can-i-put-on-a-bookshelf-besides-books">What can I put on a bookshelf besides books?</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#should-a-bookshelf-be-anchored-to-the-wall">Should a bookshelf be anchored to the wall?</a></li></ul></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#final-thoughts">Final Thoughts</a></li></ul></div></nav>


<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Start Here: The Bookshelf Styling Formula</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Good shelf styling is mostly about balance. Instead of filling each shelf edge to edge, you alternate where the visual weight sits, group objects in small sets and leave empty space so each piece can be seen. The diagram below shows the whole formula on one bookcase.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Before you style anything, secure the bookcase. The U.S. Consumer Product Safety Commission&#8217;s <a href="https://www.anchorit.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Anchor It campaign</a> says anchoring all furniture with drawers, doors and shelves to the wall prevents tip-over injuries and deaths, and a <a href="https://www.cpsc.gov/Newsroom/News-Releases/2021/Holiday-Shopping-Discounts-Are-Everywhere-Add-TV-and-Furniture-Safety-to-Your-Shopping-List" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CPSC safety release</a> advises anchoring bookcases and dressers securely to the wall and avoiding displaying items such as toys and remotes where kids might be tempted to climb. The same release notes that an average of 12,500 children are treated in emergency rooms for tip-over injuries each year.</p>



